25-DGD-161-2025/8270","a":"B","u":"fcEwL2wa6sVSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","c":"45"},{"f":"2025-05-28","i":37959.52,"e":"CNME25-DGD-147-2025/5597","a":"A","u":"W0zpP8hMgJPi0Kd8%2Brcp6w%3D%3D","c":"45"}],"q":null,"nivel":"insuficiente"}},"entidad":{"id":"ES4611001A","nombre":"Comunidad Valenciana"},"hash":"a2e03fa86bb9ebb8","ia":{"es":"Qué muestran los datos: Entre 2023 y 2025, este organismo adjudicó 103 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 26,2 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 3,9, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,0 a 5,1. En diciembre se adjudicó el 8 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 5 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 86 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.600 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que muchos contratos estén cerca del límite no indica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones legítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se repartieron de forma equitativa entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 103 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 26.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.9, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.0 to 5.1. December accounts for 8% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 86 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,600 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper actions. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts [1], [2], and [3] to see if they relate to the same service or project. Verify if multiple contracts were awarded for similar needs in the same period. Review if the awardee A has other contracts that might indicate a pattern of frequent small purchases.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["JkzKzwmXsWN4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D","O4W1N3br8Nx%2FP7lJ7Fu0SA%3D%3D","VchWnyIfEL2P66GS%2BONYvQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}